FIX FE CONFIG + INFO DIALOG SETUPS (818): reconstruct + int-type nested-table setups

The Configuration button (Configuration @0x44eae0 -> nested table @0x46918c) and the
Information button (Show_Information @0x451cc0 -> nested table @0x469b78) each dispatch a
nested screen table `code`=int(). Both trapped on wasm for the now-familiar reasons:
- Config: records 1/2 SETUP handlers were unexported raw VAs (0x44ed04 "Sound Volume",
  0x44ed24 "Save Configuration") -> reconstructed 1:1 (mirror of FUN_0044ecdc).
- Info: record 2 SETUP handler was an unexported raw VA (0x451f4c "View Credits") ->
  reconstructed (mirror of FUN_00451f0c).
- ALL setups in both tables were void(void) but the nested dispatch types them int() ->
  widened FUN_0044ecdc / FUN_00451f0c / FUN_00451f2c (and the three new ones) to int(void)
  so the call_indirect no longer traps when the dialog opens.

This makes both dialogs OPEN and NAVIGATE. The remaining record ACTIONS that enter a
sub-screen (Config 0x44e120/0x44ed44, Info 0x44d300) are larger functions -- separate
follow-up. Signature-normalization + unexported-thunk class (patches 770/816/817).

